  "query_preview": "..\nThe proximity to the monsoon trough will continue to produce regional\ninstability, allowing scattered showers and isolated thunderstorms to\ncontinue into the evening. Showers and thunder will taper down coming\ninto Saturday morning, with island showers returning near noon as\nwinds remain light and variable. Invest 93W, now a sub-low and \nlocated over the northern Marshalls, is expected to continue on its\njourney toward the Marianas and eventually break down into an open\ntrough, with some chance to bring just low-end scattered showers to\nthe area in the first half of next week.",
